; C12A  Winning 42 p. 183 (W42-p183-b); played in Hand 34, p. 113 (W42-p113-a)
; Rule, in our words: on the first trick, a bidder with exactly four trumps,
; holding the top trump and the third-highest but not the second, leads the
; top one, and does not budget the loss of a trump trick.
; Python gate (pour_bidder gate_c12, variant A): the same, under pip trumps.
; How this encoding differs: none in what it decides under pip trumps. The
; ranks are relational (the top trump is one no trump beats; the second, one
; only the top beats; the third, one only those two beat), so the same reading
; also applies under doubles trump, where the gate does not look; with no trump
; it never fires. "Exactly four" is four trump roles and no fifth.
; The book's pp. 9 and 32 (W42-p009-i, W42-p032-a) lean the other way when the
; top two trumps are not both held; p. 183 is the one place it says A.
(policy c12a-four-trumps-lead-the-double
  (fallback lowest-legal)
  (rule lead-the-double (select answer)
    (guard
      (query
        (roles (chair b) (domino top) (domino second) (domino third) (domino t3) (domino t4))
        (out top)
        (pattern
          (viewer b)
          (declarer b)
          (trick-number 1)
          (next-actor b)
          (in top q*)
          (none (roles (domino above)) (in above q*) (beats above top q*))
          (in second q*)
          (beats top second q*)
          (none (roles (domino above)) (in above q*) (beats above second q*) (not (tile above top)))
          (in third q*)
          (beats second third q*)
          (none (roles (domino above)) (in above q*) (beats above third q*)
            (not (tile above top)) (not (tile above second)))
          (own-legal top)
          (not (own-legal second))
          (own-legal third)
          (own-legal t3) (in t3 q*)
          (own-legal t4) (in t4 q*)
          (none (roles (domino fifth)) (own-legal fifth) (in fifth q*)
            (not (tile fifth top)) (not (tile fifth third)) (not (tile fifth t3)) (not (tile fifth t4))))))))
